WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.100
All right, I want to check in briefly with
you guys about the comedy of errors that are

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:13.480
Donald Trump's sworn affidavits, some of which
are arguing in Michigan that the results in

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.119
Minnesota towns prove Michigan voter fraud.

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:21.160
Now, if if you just heard me say that in your
confused, you should be confused.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.470
It makes no sense.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.920
And I'm going to explain it to you.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.460
Let's back it up a little bit.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.970
For weeks now, Trump and people around him,
including his lawyers, continue to refer to

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:37.149
supposedly sworn affidavits signed under penalty
of perjury from all sorts of different people

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:39.379
that prove that there was voter fraud.

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:43.510
Now, I've already talked to you before about
affidavits as evidence.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.310
Affidavits are a form of evidence.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.359
It could be trustworthy.

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:47.489
It might not.

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:49.690
Affidavits might be credible or they might
not.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.579
Affidavits might be admissible or they might
not.

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:54.559
They're not proof of anything per say.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:01:00.420
But when you actually start looking at some
of these affidavits, it becomes cartoonishly

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.780
farcical.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.079
Here is one such example.

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:04.140
This is just one now.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.470
They claim to have I don't know if it's thousands
or tens of thousands of these sworn affidavits

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:13.740
of people reporting wrongdoing and mathematical
anomalies or anomalies, as your preference

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.380
may be for pronunciation.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.049
But let's just look at one, OK?

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:24.740
There is an affidavit from a guy named Russell
Ramsland, who is a supposed expert on cybersecurity.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:32.200
In his affidavit, Russell attacks Dominion
Software, which is used on some voting machines.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:40.009
And it claims that there is very suspicious
activity in some towns that are in Wayne County,

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:44.950
Michigan, and in their list of towns in Wayne
County, Michigan.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:52.479
They list places like Spruce Grove Township
and Atlanta Township and Grundberg Township.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:02:00.219
All of those places are not even in Michigan,
as Jake Tapper from CNN pointed out on Twitter.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.009
Spruce Grove Township is in Minnesota.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:07.280
Atlanta Township is in Minnesota.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.440
Grundberg Township is in Minnesota.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:18.440
Now, one argument was this was supposed to
be evidence from Wayne County, Minnesota,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.090
not Wayne County, Michigan.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.030
So the everything is accurate.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.970
It's just they put me instead of men.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:31.960
And that's why all of the towns that are listed
are actually in Minnesota instead of in Michigan.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.310
That doesn't pass the sniff test because there
is no Wayne County in Minnesota.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:44.730
So what we have here is if we want to be as
charitable as possible, we have incompetence.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:51.550
If we want to maybe think of a less charitable
interpretation, these are straight up fraudulent

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:52.550
affidavits.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:58.950
The idea that they submitted these, knowing
that these are not even actually places in

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:05.420
Michigan and they were hoping to deceive courts
and hoping to move some of these bogus lawsuits

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.010
forward, we don't know.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.230
We may never know.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.670
It's increasingly irrelevant.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:15.950
This evidence supposedly from Michigan was
submitted as part of a filing in Georgia.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:22.240
The Georgia results are moving forward and
it was supposedly data from Michigan.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.330
Michigan has also now been certified and put
officially in Joe Biden's column.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.820
So it is all failing.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:34.390
But this is why, you know, we really have
to go beyond there's this idea of just throwing

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:37.910
large amounts of stuff at the wall and seeing
what sticks.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:40.100
And I've talked about this before in debate.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.430
It's something called the Gish Gallop.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:47.010
You throw a bunch of stuff out there and just
make it appear overwhelming and make it difficult

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:52.060
for whoever you're trying to convince to really
go step by step, step and refute this.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.250
The equivalent of the Gish Gallop is just
getting thousands or tens of thousands of

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:01.340
signed affidavits and, you know, holding them
up as stacks of paper as Trump cronies have

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.630
done on television and including his press
secretary, Kayleigh McEnany.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.800
But what you really need to do is not say,
wow, if there are 10000 of these things or

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.410
one hundred thousand or five thousand, whatever,
there must be something to it.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:19.709
You just have to dove in and start looking
at it and saying, OK, let's look at this one

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:23.530
affidavit and then you look at it and you
say, this really is nothing.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.620
This is really hearsay.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.280
It doesn't really tell us anything about there
being fraud.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:33.500
It's an allegation in many cases, an allegation
which, even if true, would not impact the

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.680
results of this state.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.290
And you put that aside and then you look at
the next one and then you look at this one

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:42.510
and it lists towns supposedly in Michigan
that are actually in Minnesota.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.960
And then you start eliminating it.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.490
And what do you have left?

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:50.080
You have left the realization that Joe Biden
won because he got more votes in enough states.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.080
That's really it.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:54.900
And these wee rest assured.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.560
We're not going to have to hear that much
more about affidavits for too much longer

